Processor, Core, OS thread
- A **hardware processor** is the **physical electronic chip** (the CPU) that performs computations by executing machine instructions.
- Processor can have one/multiple cores
- Each core execute one thread at a time
- Each core can execute 2 thread at a time using Hyper-Threading (Intel) or SMT(Simultaneous Multithreading) (AMD)

# When does Go switch?
Go may switch goroutines when:

- A goroutine blocks on a channel.
- A goroutine performs a blocking system call.
- A goroutine waits on a mutex.
- A goroutine calls `time.Sleep()`.
- The runtime **preempts** a goroutine that has been running for "too long."
